course: dictionary
lesson: 1514
title: A quiet place: the cemetery
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cemetery is a large area of land, often with grass and trees, where dead people are buried in graves. The words around it give clues: people «visit the cemetery» and are «buried in the cemetery».
explain: Read the clues in this sentence: «In a burial the coffin is lowered into a grave in a cemetery or churchyard.» A grave is the place a person is buried, and a cemetery is a place with many graves in it.
explain: Stories and everyday life show that a cemetery is a quiet, respectful place. People walk slowly, speak softly and leave flowers. Gravestones there can tell us about people of the past.
explain: Some people use a different word for the same place. «Memorial park» is an American word for a cemetery. When you see a new word, ask: could it mean the same thing as a word I already know?
fact: A cemetery is a large area of land where dead people are buried in graves.
fact: «Cemetery» is a noun, and its plural is «cemeteries».
fact: «Memorial park» is an American word for a cemetery.
fact: People often visit a cemetery quietly and leave flowers on the graves.
fact: Gravestones in a cemetery can tell us about people who lived long ago.
exercise: «In a burial the coffin is lowered into a grave in a cemetery or churchyard.» Where is the coffin lowered? | Into a swimming pool | Into a big box on a train | *Into a grave in a cemetery or churchyard | Onto the roof of a house
exercise: «Picture the cemetery after Grandad's funeral.» Ellie throws a little handful of soil as her goodbye. Where does this happen? | *At the cemetery, after Grandad's funeral | At the seaside | In a school hall | In a swimming pool
exercise: What is a cemetery? | A big building where people play games | *A large area of land where dead people are buried in graves | A shop that sells flowers | A kind of tall tree
test: «Memorial park» is an American word for what? | *A cemetery | A playground | A museum | A library
test: In history lessons, what can gravestones in a cemetery tell us? | *About people of the past | The best time to go swimming | Which shops are open this weekend | How to cook a good soup
exam: People visit the cemetery quietly and leave flowers; what does «respectful» suggest? | Very loud and fast | Happy and playing games | *Showing care and politeness | Dirty and wet
